{"title":"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 14","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>\tLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/5/92523d7260525b75406c593cb650e9076c0b9af8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = \\int_{0}^{x^{2}} \\cos t \\, dt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"150\" height=\"48\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/a/bbad379658bd32e9b6479bbd666b93a96e6b48ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f&#39;(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p><p>\t<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc042cac951d5a7f5d5af9bc4655eccc1d7b5f8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ f&#39;(x) = \\cos(x^{2})  \\quad \t\\textbf{(B)}\\ f&#39;(x) = 2x\\sin(x^{2})  \\quad \t\\textbf{(C)}\\ f&#39;(x) = -2x\\sin(x^{2})  \\quad \t\\textbf{(D)}\\ f&#39;(x) = 2x\\cos(x^{2})  \\quad \t\\textbf{(E)}\\ f&#39;(x) = \\sin(x^{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"918\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_14&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the First Fundamental Theorem of Calculus and the chain rule,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/0/920f0df24e52286e3db9848668b6165c5bdd2570.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{d}{dx} \\int_{0}^{x^{2}} \\cos t \\, dt = \\cos(x^{2}) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx}\\left[ x^{2} \\right] - \\cos(0) \\cdot \\frac{d}{dx} \\left[ 0 \\right] \\implies \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ f&#39;(x) = 2x\\cos(x^{2})}.\\]\" width=\"614\" height=\"46\" />\n</p><p>~Blosp\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest\">2026 TMTA Calculus</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 15\">Problem 15</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Calculus_Contest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 TMTA High School Calculus Contest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_TMTA_High_School_Cal